{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/39871-dragons-and-changeling","id":39871,"title":"Dragons and Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-31T02:56:55-08:00","id":39871,"title":"Dragons and Changeling","content":"This is something I've been mulling over since I read the short story in Equinox Road about the Poet Who Walked on the Sun. There's a bit where he describes the circling gulls as &quot;big as dragons from the Forgotten Days&quot;. Later on in Equinox Road, one of the sample Domains is populated by Drakes, who, the author is quick to assert, are not true dragons. Nevertheless, these Drakes are possibly something other than Changeling or Fae (there's a rumour that they might be Changelings that have sworn a pledge to become a Drake, but it's unconfirmed as no one has ever returned from a meeting with the eldest Drakes). Fae is entirely wild and strange enough that dragons could simply be True Fae adopting particularly grand and powerful forms, but there's a certain level of reverence being directed in the direction of the concept &quot;dragon&quot; here that really does make me wonder. Dragons exist, or existed, there's no doubt about that. But the way the Poet talks it's like they've become something akin to a myth even for the True Fae. Maybe they were a form the Fae used to take, but no longer do. Maybe they're a kind of Ur-Fae, or a form only the greatest Fae are allowed or able to use. Or maybe they're something separate from the Fae themselves, an independent creature (although maybe still attached to the Wyrd somehow) that were so strong even the Fae show them a level of respect.<br /> <br /> Since I feel that dragons slot perfectly into the fairy tale mood of Changeling, and watching the latest Hobbit has rekindled a bit of love for the giant scaly beasts, I've been mulling over different ways to bring them into my current chronicle. A token of some kind made of dragon bone (all the Deverry books I've read over the years want me to make it a flute) seems like a good way to start, and possibly serve as a bit of foreshadowing if I want an honest-to-goodness dragon to crop up at some point.<br /> <br /> I'm ignoring Dzarumazh a bit here, but he does deserve a mention. For one, he's basically all the proof needed for the &quot;dragons exist&quot; statement above. For another, he's clearly a sign that the True Fae can adopt the form of a dragon, although, since the Fae can't create anything original, there's always a chance that he's just stealing the idea from something older rather than from human myths.<br /> <br /> So anyway, what do people think about dragons in Changeling? Has anyone tried including one into their Chronicle? How would you all go about running them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T03:43:40-08:00","id":39894,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;Dragons? Please. I know we're a bunch of fairy tale rejects, but dragons are firmly in the realm of bullshit. Anyone telling you otherwise either saw a big hobgoblin or is trying to sell you something.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I do like the idea of something lurking in Arcadia other than the True Fae and Hobgoblins, but am not sure how to use them (perhaps the morning will bring inspiration; it's 4AM at the moment). Is there territory in Arcadia other than the realms of the True Fae (since the Fae are both themselves and their lands), or would Dragons be relegated to the Hedge? There's also the Draconic seeming, which at the very least promises Fae taking the shape of dragons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T03:55:41-08:00","id":39899,"title":"","content":"Equinox Road has something about dead domains, if I remember right. The wilds of Arcadia with no ruling Fae. There's certainly potential for them to be there, somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T09:26:40-08:00","id":40027,"title":"","content":"There's an actual dragon in Grim Fears. He's a True Fae and an enormously powerful one. I think you're overthinking the bit about drakes. Yes they're not true dragons, but it never says anything about the lack of dragons in Arcadia. I think the reason it made a point about Drakes not being true dragons is because true dragons are true fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T09:40:18-08:00","id":40034,"title":"","content":"On the previous incarnation of these forums, I wrote up a goblin market called the Hoard, for obvious reasons: it was the cavernous treasury-lair of a dragon, deep in the Hedge, where the slaves of the dragon would sell anything they could get away with while the master was away.<br /> <br /> Also, in a chronicle that never panned out, a great Asiatic dragon was to appear in the character's dreams (being so vast that it could not take physical form, it lived between dreams, and sometimes intruded upon them). It was going to set a bunch of plot threads in motion, including convincing one changeling to have a child and give it to him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/39871-dragons-and-changeling?p=40027#post40027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the reason it made a point about Drakes not being true dragons is because true dragons are true fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems awfully reductive. Dragons are dragons; some dragons are Fae, some are not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 12-31-2013, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T09:50:11-08:00","id":40038,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I phrased that badly. It should say &quot;true faerie dragons&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T09:52:02-08:00","id":40040,"title":"","content":"I find myself reminded of the issues NWoD sometimes has with &quot;when you say demon, which one of five different supernatural things are you referring to?&quot; Same with dragons. There's plenty of things in NWoD that can get <i>called</i> dragons. Awakened Dragons, shapeshifting spirits, giant hobgoblins, True Fae, etc.<br /> <br /> For my own part, one of the key True Fae (the Collector) has a favored Actor form known as Valrauth the Grand, or Jianlong the Crocodile Dragon, depending on where you are. The classic dragon traits (big, powerful, cunning, with a fondness for riddles) certainly map well to the True Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T16:13:48-08:00","id":40198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/39871-dragons-and-changeling?p=40027#post40027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an actual dragon in Grim Fears. He's a True Fae and an enormously powerful one. I think you're overthinking the bit about drakes. Yes they're not true dragons, but it never says anything about the lack of dragons in Arcadia. I think the reason it made a point about Drakes not being true dragons is because true dragons are true fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did mention Dzarumazh in my first post, and included the fact that it was pretty clear that any of the gentry could be a dragon. I don't think that necessarily discredits the idea that dragons could be something separate that the Fae are just copying, but I also concede that what the dragon actually is becomes fairly immaterial in a game with as few limitations as Changeling. It's a dragon, which is about as much as the Changelings ever need to discover. Hobgoblins and the True Fae can be literally anything you want, after all. I'm more interested in what ideas people have for using dragons in chronicles.<br /> <br /> The idea of the hoard as a Goblin Market is really, really cool. I can just imagine the frantic scurry to get out of there once the dragon has been spotted on its way back home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T16:46:25-08:00","id":40219,"title":"","content":"Considering the cross-pollination between Changeling and Mage it's probably a reference to the dragons from awakened mythology. They appear more definitely in Dancers in Dusk where the Dragon Dreams are mentioned as one of the less-encountered Morpheans. I'd probably probably be more annoyed with this is it wasn't for the fact that Mage is pretty stubborn on not explaining what the dragons were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T17:25:54-08:00","id":40251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/39871-dragons-and-changeling?p=39894#post39894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>&quot;Dragons? Please. I know we're a bunch of fairy tale rejects, but dragons are firmly in the realm of bullshit. Anyone telling you otherwise either saw a big hobgoblin or is trying to sell you something.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I do like the idea of something lurking in Arcadia other than the True Fae and Hobgoblins, but am not sure how to use them (perhaps the morning will bring inspiration; it's 4AM at the moment). Is there territory in Arcadia other than the realms of the True Fae (since the Fae are both themselves and their lands), or would Dragons be relegated to the Hedge? There's also the Draconic seeming, which at the very least promises Fae taking the shape of dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Fae will take any shape that deals with Title and allows thrive on conflict.<br /> <br /> Given the case, I wouldn't be surprise if you had a Fae that mimicked the Uratha or the Kindred along with various Dragon analogs. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T04:19:33-08:00","id":40449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/39871-dragons-and-changeling?p=40251#post40251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Fae will take any shape that deals with Title and allows thrive on conflict.<br /> <br /> Given the case, I wouldn't be surprise if you had a Fae that mimicked the Uratha or the Kindred along with various Dragon analogs.</div> </div> </div> </div>don't we have a vampiric True Fae as a version of Bloody Mary, with a all Covenant focused around her?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><b